      "writtenOn": "2024-06-04T14:24:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, basically, we skip the rollback protection performed using the instance.img if the guest either supports deferred RBP or has a hardcoded RBP in pvmfw.\n\nTo avoid duplicating the validation of `verified_boot_data.rollback_index` (which must already be non-zero for RKP VM, at this point) and to prefer self-documenting code over long comments, would you mind introducing another local flag:\n```\nlet rollback_protection_done \u003d dice_inputs.rkp_vm_marker;\n```\nallowing, here:\n```\nif defer_rollback_protection {\n    if verified_boot_data.rollback_index \u003d\u003d 0 { ... }\n} else if !rollback_protection_done {\n    let (recorded_entry, mut instance_img, header_index) \u003d ...;\n    ...\n}\n```\n?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 165,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 165,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d5fccbf51354934267f26bb78507b66a96cc1bbb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "443ab56f_7c246b4a",
