      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-06T07:19:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do understand the need for a slightly generic capability than `dice_inputs.rkp_vm_marker`, I think `rollback_protection_done` would be too generic and will need to set true even after instance.img based checks (becuse logically `rollback_protection_done` is done by then too) but in that case `rollback_protection_done` is not useful (no consumer), so why add a variable at all. Something like `version_check_done_against_hardcoded_value` would have been more suitable, but I dont think we really need that variable.\n\n\nInstead in a different patch, I will move the rkpvm version check below to this block. Ensuring all rollback protection is done in these these sections. \n```\nif defer_rollback_protection {\n    if verified_boot_data.rollback_index \u003d\u003d 0 { ... }\n} else if verified_boot_data.has_capability(Capability::RemoteAttest) {\n    // Check against hardcoded value\n} else {\n   // Fallback to instance.img based rollback protection\n}\n```\n\nWhile this special-cases `Capability::RemoteAttest` here, it reduces the specificity from the other section of main.rs. \n\nThanks for your suggestions.",
      "parentUuid": "443ab56f_7c246b4a",
